I'm locking this thread subject, which means that people can start new =
threads, but messages will be held if it replies to this one.

spt
(for the chairs)

> On Oct 15, 2026, at 15:42, Ken Kubota <ietf@kenkubota.de> wrote:
>=20
> In response to your message from this thread: =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/p25hQE5OZ97uNbNfDUdPIZqJXZk/
>=20
>=20
>> Perhaps because Dr. Bersteins concerns have been heard and found not =
to have consensus.  Honest people can disagree, and we all lose =
sometimes.  Not everything is a conspiracy.
>=20
> 4. Concerns: Both Professor Bernstein's concerns and mine remain =
unaddressed. "My objections were never addressed, including by the NSA, =
which responded to an earlier email from me via NSA employee William =
Layton: =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/tls/vFu5iq8gPQFByj4L0hkCEAJUR9I/" =
[1]
>=20
> 5. Consensus: While the Working Group (WG) Chairs claimed consensus, =
it was evident that none existed. [1] Furthermore, none of the chairs =
holding academic positions approved the draft. [1] Professor Bernstein's =
concerns do not require a consensus among themselves; rather, the =
*draft* requires a consensus. The distinction is clear: Concerns must be =
addressed, not merely voted upon for their own sake.
>=20
> 6. Lack of Transparency: Although the WG Chairs explicitly stated that =
there was 70% approval, they have refused to provide the underlying =
evidence. [1] This contradicts the IETF's stated commitment to =
transparency.
>=20
> I have never used the term "conspiracy."
> "The term "conspiracy theory" is terminology from the field of =
psychological warfare.
> Professor Mausfeld (Christian-Albrechts-University Kiel, Department of =
Psychology) once stated the famous quote: "Besonders beliebt sind =
'Querfront' und 'Verschw=C3=B6rungstheorie'."
> [=E2=80=A6]
> The trick is to associate any critique, which aims at the center of =
power, with something that is socially ostracized, in order to sabotage =
the criticism.
> He calls such terms (e.g., "conspiracy theory") "denunciation terms," =
used to poison the debate.
> If you need to resort to denunciation terms, you are actually =
supporting my position." [2]
> In a fair debate, such terms should be avoided.
>=20
> Are you expressing your personal view, or are you representing an =
official/semi-official position of Cisco as an employee [3]?
>=20
> What is your proposal to resolve this conflict of interest?
> "In December 2024, a Cisco employee wrote the following: "There are =
people whose cryptographic expertise I cannot doubt who say that pure =
ML-KEM is the right trade-off for them, and more importantly for my =
employer, that's what they're willing to buy. Hence, Cisco will =
implement it; I am essentially just asking for code points." Certainly =
"willing to buy" is a statement about funding, evidently from a source =
large enough to dictate Cisco actions, evidently from a source asking =
for non-hybrids, evidently from "people whose cryptographic expertise I =
cannot doubt"; if that source isn't NSA, who is it?" [4]
>=20
> Kind regards,
>=20
> Ken Kubota
>=20
> ____________________________________________________
>=20
> Ken Kubota
> https://doi.org/10.4444/100
>=20
>=20
> [1] =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/OrvxKgjrEOMb95KAWoJYSilDxiY/
>=20
> [2] =
https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ssh/Xx0yHcp2-z2A7oiELB-gxzgWs9k/
>=20
> [3] https://datatracker.ietf.org/person/Richard%20Barnes
> "Richard Barnes is a Distinguished Engineer in the Collaboration =
CTO=E2=80=99s office at Cisco."
> "rlb@ipv.sx"
>=20
> [4] https://blog.cr.yp.to/20251004-weakened.html
>=20
>=20
>=20
>> Am 15.10.2026 um 17:54 schrieb Richard Barnes <rlb@ipv.sx>:
>>=20
>> On Thu, Oct 15, 2026 at 11:01=E2=80=AFAM Ken Kubota =
<ietf@kenkubota.de <mailto:ietf@kenkubota.de>> wrote:
>>>=20
>>> 1. Why is former NSA lifetime employee Deb Cooley, now serving as =
Security Area Director, forcing through a document [1] that deflects =
Professor Bernstein's concerns [2]?=20
>>=20
>> Perhaps because Dr. Bersteins concerns have been heard and found not =
to have consensus.  Honest people can disagree, and we all lose =
sometimes.  Not everything is a conspiracy.
>=20
